# Written by `next dev` on every run, and swept into two feature commits by `git add -A` before
# this line existed. AGENTS.md is Next 16 telling an agent its APIs differ from the training
# data, and CLAUDE.md is one line pointing at it.
#
# Ignored rather than committed because apps/app/CLAUDE.md changes the instructions every agent
# reads in this directory, and that should be a decision somebody makes on purpose rather than a
# passenger on whatever feature branch ran the dev server last. Their own text argues for
# committing them; that argument is worth having, and this line is where to start it.
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
